*************
Compilation
*************

gcc -Wall -pedantic -std=c99 -o a2LUHN a2LUHN.c

**************************
Running the program
**************************

When the program is run, a short intro will open first
The user will then be prompted to enter a 16 digit credit card number
Enter the number without any characters between the numbers
If the number is too large, small, or contains a character the program will quit
Once the number is inputed the program will output if the number was valid or not

**************************
Known Limitations
**************************

Cannot remove '-' characters that are included with alot of credit card numbers
	-> the program will just quit, saying that there was a char entered
Has to re-run in order to enter a new number
No input that I could find would cause the program to crash
